# Code owners are automatically requested for review on pull requests that touch matching paths,
# and the branch ruleset can require their approval.
#
# Today every line names the same person, so this file changes nothing about who reviews what.
# It exists so that the moment a second maintainer joins, the sensitive surfaces below can be routed
# to a specific reviewer by editing one line here instead of relying on everyone remembering.
#
# The handle is the maintainer's current GitHub account. It may move to a personal (non-employer)
# account before or after the first release; when that happens, every line here must change
# together, and the ruleset's "require code owner review" setting will pick it up automatically.
#
# Syntax: the LAST matching pattern wins, so keep the catch-all first and the specific paths after it.

# Everything, by default.
* @mihail-alexe-nutanix

# CI and release automation: a change here can publish to npm or run with elevated tokens.
/.github/workflows/ @mihail-alexe-nutanix

# This file itself: whoever owns CODEOWNERS controls review routing.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @mihail-alexe-nutanix

# Package identity, dependency surface and the lockfile that CI installs from.
/package.json @mihail-alexe-nutanix
/package-lock.json @mihail-alexe-nutanix

# The Vite integration is the core of the fork and the part most likely to break user builds.
/src/vite/ @mihail-alexe-nutanix

# Legal and security policy: changes here are never "just docs".
/License.md @mihail-alexe-nutanix
/SECURITY.md @mihail-alexe-nutanix
